      "message": "This will:\n* Create a thread\n* Connect to perfetto (which requires the SElinux permission)\n\nDo we want to do it in every circumstance? Specifically:\n\n1. For /system/bin/servicemanager.\n2. What about for the vendor service manager?\n3. What about the hwservice manager?\n4. What about the `servicemanager.recovery`?\n\nFor 1, we obviously want to connect and we\u0027re changing SELinux rules. Good.\n\nFor 2 and 3, SELinux should prevent it from connecting to perfetto. I would either make the SELinux change or avoid initialization (it\u0027s fine to execute the PERFETTO_TE macros without initialization, they will be noops).\n\nFor 4, I\u0027m not sure how servicemanager.recovery is used. Is perfetto `traced` running in that context?",
